50,3,1,talk,Midori,,"The candidates are A: Home Follow-Up, B: Day Rehab, C: Chronic Care, and D: Perinatal Support. I lean toward D.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"A has proven value in readmissions, but D is safer given the booking and reporting issues.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Misaki,,D is the only one that fits our staffing. Midwifery has slack; therapy and nursing are exhausted.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Shion,,D is the most viable. It uses existing slack and avoids the funding void of off-site visits.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Shizue,,D is a good fit. It avoids the parking crisis of a Day Unit and the data delays of Chronic Care.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, do you think the Perinatal service would suffer from the reporting gaps you found?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"Less so than Chronic Care, which requires those external data agreements Shizue mentioned.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, would the Perinatal classes overload the rooms?","{""words"":8,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Shion,,"If they are scheduled efficiently, it's better than a full Day Rehab unit which would kill the car park.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, as long as they aren't all mid-morning, it should be manageable.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Midori,,I'm voting for D. It's the most harmonious choice for the staff.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. D is the most sustainable.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Misaki,,D is my vote. It's the only one the roster can actually support.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Shion,,I vote D. It's the only option that doesn't create a financial or staffing deficit.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I also vote for D. It's the least likely to seize up our infrastructure.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
